Chapter 39: The Phantom in the Canopy
High above the dark, purple-tinged fog of Outpost Rift #42, Kaelen moved through the canopy like an invisible ghost.
Denser black pine branches swayed under the damp wind, but Kaelen’s boots made zero sound as they touched the moss-slick bark. His active skill—[Phantom Kinetic Cloak]—was running at maximum efficiency. To the sensors, thermal tracking units, and monster senses in the forest, Kaelen Vance simply did not exist.
Below him, in the muddy western ravine, Renna’s voice echoed through the mist.
"HOLD THE CHOKE-POINT! TOBIAS, WATCH THE CANOPY!"
Four Iron-Claw Stalkers (Tier-C)—six-foot reptilian beasts with razor-sharp chitin claws—were scrambling down the tree trunks toward Renna’s flank. Further back, two ten-foot Grave-Vine Abominations (Tier-C Elite)—masses of writhing, thorn-covered tendrils wrapped around heavy bone cores—were preparing to unleash a volley of toxic spine-barbs straight into Mina’s exposed back.
Too many for them to handle at once, Kaelen calculated silently, his [Hive-Mind Synapse] mapping the precise trajectories of every beast in a two-hundred-meter radius. If I let both Abominations fire, Renna’s shield line collapses.
Kaelen didn't drop to the ground. He didn't roar, and he didn't give a warning.
He activated his speed skill:
"[Lightning-Phase Blitz]!"
ZAP!
Coated in a suppressed arc of electric-blue lighting, Kaelen’s 102 Agility accelerated his physical frame into a blinding, silent streak across the upper canopy.
He materialized directly above the lead Grave-Vine Abomination.
Falling forty feet straight down through the fog, Kaelen brought his right fist—backed by 101 Strength and reinforced by his sub-dermal Kinetic-Void Bracers—crashing down into the monster’s central bone core.
BOOOOOOM!
The compact, electric-charged impact detonated with surgical precision inside the beast's chest. The three-ton Tier-C Elite Abomination didn't even have time to shriek; its central core shattered into fine dust, its thorn-covered tendrils collapsing into a lifeless heap of rotting plant matter.
Before the second Abomination could register the sudden death of its mate, Kaelen phase-shifted across the damp grass, driving an open-palm electric strike straight into its central eye cluster.
CRACK-BOOM!
The second Tier-C Elite Abomination exploded into a shower of green sap and bone fragments.
Kaelen didn't pause to admire the kill. Moving like a tempest in the shadows, he blurred through the lower branches, executing a sequence of lightning-fast, silent neck-snaps and kinetic palm strikes on the surrounding eight Iron-Claw Stalkers.
THUD. THUD. THUD. THUD.
In less than six seconds, the entire ambushing wave was slaughtered. Kaelen intentionally left three wounded, low-tier Stalkers crawling through the mud near the ravine entrance—just enough for Renna, Tobias, and Mina to handle safely without pushing their physical limits.
Kaelen pressed his bare palms onto the two dead Abominations for half a second.
"[Dissect & Assimilate]!"
Dark gray vapor erupted, devouring the carcasses silently before sweeping two Tier-C Elite Cores and a dozen pristine thorn-barbs into his spatial inventory.
With the threat to Squad 4 neutralized, Kaelen turned his gaze toward the eastern perimeter of the forest.
His [Low-Light Spatial Perception] picked up the energy signatures of Ironclad Squad 2.
Senior Officer Marcus and his three corporate operatives were standing behind a high rock ridge three hundred meters away, holding thermal rangefinders and watching the fog with arrogant, amused grins.
"The auxiliary reserves should be wiped out by now," one of Marcus's men scoffed, adjusting his tactical rifle. "The Grave-Vine Abominations were right on top of their shield line."
Marcus chuckled, flexing his heavy, polished kinetic power-armor. "Let them die. When the municipal report comes out, we'll log it as an unexpected monster surge. We take the Rift Core, collect the full bounty, and Anvil Ridge loses their reserve status."
Suddenly, the air behind Marcus grew deathly cold.
The temperature dropped instantly. The surrounding purple fog swirled backward as if repelled by a massive, invisible pressure.
Marcus’s smile froze. His tactical sensor suit began wailing with frantic, shrill warning alarms.
WARNING! UNKNOWN APEX PREDATOR DETECTED!
THREAT LEVEL: UNMEASURABLE!
"What the—" Marcus gasped, whipping his heavy broadsword around.
There was no sound of footsteps. No mana signature. Only a dark, towering silhouette stepping out of the dense fog three feet in front of him.
The figure wore a faded, dark hood pulled low over its face. The eyes beneath the hood held zero emotion—only a cold, abyss-like abyss that made Marcus’s blood run completely cold.
"W-Who are you?!" Marcus yelled, his voice cracking with sudden, uncontrollable panic as he raised his heavy kinetic broadsword. "This is an official Vanguard Guild operation! Identify yourself!"
Kaelen didn't answer. He didn't utter a single word.
He simply stepped forward and swung a simple, compact right straight punch directly at Marcus's chest.
Marcus raised his high-grade, corporate-funded kinetic shoulder plate to block the hit.
BOOOOOOOOOOM!
The impact sounded like a heavy artillery shell detonating at point-blank range.
The multi-million-credit kinetic power-armor—built to withstand impacts from Tier-B dungeon bosses—shattered like cheap glass. The alloy plates buckled, the internal energy coils exploded in a shower of sparks, and the massive kinetic shockwave blasted Marcus off his feet, sending him crashing through three massive pine trees before slamming into the muddy earth sixty feet away.
Marcus coughed up a spray of blood, clutching his ruined, shattered shoulder armor in absolute, hysterical terror.
The three remaining Ironclad operatives dropped their tactical rifles, their faces pale as death, their legs shaking violently as they looked at the hooded phantom standing in the crater.
"R-RUN! IT'S AN ANCIENT RIFT PHANTOM!" Marcus screamed frantically, scrambling backward through the mud on his knees. "RETREAT! RETREAT OUT OF THE RIFT!"
The four Ironclad operatives turned and fled toward the rift entrance like terrified rats, abandoning their positions, their equipment, and the mission entirely.
Kaelen stood alone in the quiet forest, lowering his fist as his Kinetic-Void Bracers hummed softly under his sleeves.
He looked down at his hand, then turned back toward the western ravine where Renna’s shield was ringing with the sound of combat against the remaining three Stalkers.
"Sabotage cleared," Kaelen whispered, stepping back into the shadows of the canopy.
